---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import '../styles/approved-pages.css';
import '../styles/approved-start-here.css';
---
<Layout title="Start Here" masthead={false}>
<div class="approved-page start-here-page">
<section class="start-opening">
<div class="start-introduction">
<h1>Start <em>Here.</em>
</h1>
<p>You can begin with a machine, a programming idea or a question. Choose what you want to do. The shared explanations are here when you need them; you do not have to complete them before starting a system track.</p>
</div>
<nav class="start-route-index" aria-label="Choose your starting point">
<a href="#make-game">Make a game</a>
<a href="#programming">Explore programming ideas</a>
<a href="#programs-run">Understand how programs run</a>
<a href="#craft">Explore game-making ideas</a>
<a href="#history">Explore computing history</a>
<a href="#teaching">Parents and teachers</a>
</nav>
</section>
<section class="start-route with-evidence" id="make-game" aria-labelledby="make-game-title">
<div class="start-route-heading">
<h2 id="make-game-title">Make A Game</h2>
</div>
<div class="start-route-body">
<h3>Choose a machine and start building</h3>
<p>Browse the systems with lessons available and choose a language route. You can start here as a beginner; completing <a href="/foundations/">Foundations</a> or another system track is not a prerequisite.</p>
<a class="action" href="/systems/"><span>Find a system with lessons</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
</a>
</div>
<div class="start-evidence">
<figure class="capture" style="--capture-width:416px;--capture-height:312px"><img src="/images/learning/c64.png" width="416" height="312" alt="Safe Cracker, a complete guessing game from the Commodore 64 BASIC lessons"><figcaption>Safe Cracker · Commodore 64 · BASIC. One of the games you can learn to build.</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
</section>
<section class="start-route text-route" id="programming" aria-labelledby="programming-title">
<div class="start-route-heading">
<h2 id="programming-title">Explore Programming Ideas</h2>
</div>
<div class="start-route-body">
<h3>Start with the programming concepts</h3>
<p>
<a href="/foundations/">Foundations</a> uses pseudocode to explain instructions, variables, decisions and loops without choosing a machine or language. Follow its guided examples, or return when a lesson raises a question.</p>
<a class="action" href="/foundations/basics"><span>Explore The Basics</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
</a>
</div>
</section>
<section class="start-route text-route" id="programs-run" aria-labelledby="programs-run-title">
<div class="start-route-heading">
<h2 id="programs-run-title">Understand How Programs Run</h2>
</div>
<div class="start-route-body">
<h3>Look beneath the language</h3>
<p>
<a href="/from-the-metal">From the Metal</a> explores programming choices through concrete machine behaviour. See why an approach helps, what it costs and where comparisons with modern systems have limits.</p>
<a class="action" href="/from-the-metal"><span>Read the programming essays</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
</a>
</div>
</section>
<section class="start-route with-evidence" id="craft" aria-labelledby="craft-title">
<div class="start-route-heading">
<h2 id="craft-title">Explore Game-Making Ideas</h2>
</div>
<div class="start-route-body">
<h3>Connect maths and game design</h3>
<p>
<a href="/craft">The Craft</a> is developing shared explanations for game-making. <a href="/craft/maths-for-games">Maths for Games</a> and <a href="/craft/game-feel">Game Feel</a> have their first lessons published, with more sequences to follow.</p>
<a class="action" href="/craft"><span>Explore The Craft</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
</a>
</div>
<div class="start-evidence">
<figure class="capture" style="--capture-width:352px;--capture-height:296px"><img src="/images/learning/dice.png" width="352" height="296" alt="A BASIC dice experiment showing six totals and a coloured frequency chart"><figcaption>Maths for Games · roll, count, compare. An experiment from the published lessons.</figcaption>
</figure>
</div>
</section>
<section class="start-route text-route" id="history" aria-labelledby="history-title">
<div class="start-route-heading">
<h2 id="history-title">Explore Computing History</h2>
</div>
<div class="start-route-body">
<h3>Follow the machines and their stories</h3>
<p>
<a href="/vault">The Vault</a> connects computers, games, people, companies and culture. You can explore it without following a programming course.</p>
<a class="action" href="/vault"><span>Browse the encyclopaedia</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
</a>
</div>
</section>
<section class="start-route text-route" id="teaching" aria-labelledby="teaching-title">
<div class="start-route-heading">
<h2 id="teaching-title">Parents And Teachers</h2>
</div>
<div class="start-route-body">
<h3>Help someone else learn</h3>
<p>Find guidance for working through the material together, choosing a starting point and supporting questions and experiments.</p>
<a class="action" href="/teaching"><span>Read the teaching guide</span><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="24" height="24" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12h15m-6-6 6 6-6 6" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2"/></svg>
</a>
</div>
</section>
<div class="start-secondary">
<p>Want to see how these fit together? <a href="/curriculum">Explore the curriculum map</a>, <a href="/about">read the longer story</a>, or <a href="/contribute">help build what is missing</a>.</p>
</div>
</div>
</Layout>
